# Copy this file to ~/.config/workspaces-host/credentials and fill in
# whatever you have - leave the rest blank, or delete lines you don't
# need. `workspaces-host-update` actually creates this file for you
# automatically, from this exact template, the first time you run it
# and none exists yet - so you may already have a real copy waiting for
# you at that path; this tracked copy is just the reference template.
#
# This is a plain KEY=value file, not Nix - no `age-keygen`, no `sops
# --encrypt`, nothing to install first. Just fill in the values below.
#
# Never commit this file (or your real copy of it) anywhere. Your real
# copy lives at ~/.config/workspaces-host/credentials, entirely outside
# this repository - `git pull`/`workspaces-host-update` never touch it -
# and `workspaces-host-update` sets it to mode 600 (readable only by
# you) every time it runs. Nix itself never reads this file directly;
# `workspaces-host-update` reads it, wires everything up (your git
# identity, and each key/token into the same scoped-per-command
# mechanism this setup already uses for AI CLI credentials - see
# README's "Setting up your credentials" section), re-activates your
# profile, and finishes by running `doctor` to confirm it all worked.

# Your name and email, used for every git commit.
GIT_NAME=
GIT_EMAIL=

# A GitHub/GitLab personal access token (create one under Settings ->
# Developer settings on either site - a short-lived one, with an
# expiration date, is safer than a permanent one). Used by `gh`/`glab`,
# and by anything else that reads these variables.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITLAB_TOKEN=

# API keys for the AI harness CLIs this setup provisions (Claude Code,
# OpenAI's Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, aider - see README's "Setting up AI
# harness credentials" section). Leave any of these blank for a CLI
# you'd rather log in to directly instead - Claude Code and Gemini CLI
# both support their own browser-based `login` command.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
